  "verbalization": "Allithiamine is shown to have targets that are involved in the regulation of M19-MEL through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Allithiamine interacts with proteins such as Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP and VMRC-LCP, which are both targets of complex molecules with structural similarities to (1R,4aR,4bS,7R,10aS)-7-ethenyl-1,4a,7-trimethyl-3,4,4b,5,6,9,10,10a-octahydro-2H-phenanthrene-1-carboxylic acid and its isomer. These compounds are implicated in the regulation of M19-MEL, as they are shown to have targets that ultimately lead to M19-MEL. The scores for these interactions are consistent, indicating a potential role for Allithiamine in modulating the activity of these pathways. The evidence suggests that Allithiamine may influence the function of M19-MEL through its interaction with these targets, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated."
